---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../components/ProjectCard.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Technical Project Delivery | SCT Engineering Works" description="Requirements, planning, design reviews, risk, supplier coordination, verification, documentation, commissioning, and production transfer for mechanical systems." alternatePath="/fr/conduite-de-projet/">
  <header class="container page-hero">
    <p class="section-kicker">Capability track 03</p>
    <h1>Technical project delivery</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">Precision projects fail at interfaces as often as they fail in calculations. I structure the path from requirements to acceptance across mechanics, controls, instrumentation, suppliers, testing, and production.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section container" data-reveal>
    <div class="capability-grid">
      <article class="capability-panel"><h3>Scope and requirements</h3><p>Clarify functions, constraints, interfaces, deliverables, decision owners, success measures, and acceptance evidence.</p></article>
      <article class="capability-panel"><h3>Planning and flow</h3><p>Sequence technical work, expose dependencies, manage milestones and priorities, and coordinate multidisciplinary execution using Kanban principles.</p></article>
      <article class="capability-panel"><h3>Risk and quality</h3><p>Connect design reviews, technical risks, verification activities, non-conformities, and acceptance criteria to the project plan.</p></article>
      <article class="capability-panel"><h3>Stakeholders and transfer</h3><p>Coordinate specialists, suppliers, production teams, demonstrations, documentation, commissioning, and structured handover.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" data-reveal>
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">Delivery evidence</span><h2>Technical leadership anchored in outputs.</h2></div><p>The focus is not ceremony. It is making the next engineering decision visible, owned, supported by evidence, and connected to acceptance.</p></div>
    <table class="evidence-table"><thead><tr><th>Project signal</th><th>Delivery contribution</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Cross-functional coordination</strong></td><td>Led a 6-person mechanics, controls, and instrumentation team using Kanban and design reviews</td><td>National reference machine delivered at &lt; 20 nm uncertainty</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Production transfer</strong></td><td>Coordinated R&D, production, suppliers, test protocols, acceptance criteria, and technical demonstrations</td><td>Calibration reference deployed across 2 sites</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Operational improvement</strong></td><td>Introduced SPC monitoring and data-led calibration interval optimization</td><td>15% equipment downtime reduction</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="section light-section" data-reveal><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">Relevant work</span><h2>Delivery case studies.</h2></div><p>These examples show coordinated technical work from requirements and design through verification and operational use.</p></div><div class="project-grid">
    <ProjectCard eyebrow="Multidisciplinary delivery" title="National reference form metrology" description="A multi-year special-purpose machine delivered across mechanics, controls, instrumentation, and measurement science." href="/projects/national-form-metrology/" result="6-person team" />
    <ProjectCard eyebrow="Industrialization" title="3D optical calibration reference" description="A repeatable calibration solution moved from concept to use at two production sites." href="/projects/3d-calibration-reference/" result="2-site deployment" />
  </div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>

